// `Int / Int` as the operand of a comparison in a module fn. Same refusal as
// int_true_division.rvl (issue #2201), reached through a different statement:
// the enclosing `>` would refuse its Float operand by the relational-operator
// message, so the reference's `_V3Emitter._bin_expr` refuses an Int `/`
// operand by its own name first. The line-coverage gate drives both sides over
// it here; that is the only way that operand check's raise runs. Both answers
// are asserted by tests/test_selfhost_emit_wasm.py
// (test_int_true_division_is_refused_by_name_on_both_sides).
pub fn big(a: Int, b: Int) -> Bool { return a / b > 1.0 }
